cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  SCEPTRE: Separator-tree Conformal Estimation for Provable
  Tamper-Resilient Elimination
message: If you use this software or the SSC dataset, please cite it.
type: software
authors:
  - name: SCEPTRE authors
repository-code: https://github.com/USERNAME/sceptre
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
date-released: '2026-08-24'
keywords:
  - false data injection
  - load frequency control
  - power system security
  - conformal prediction
  - control barrier function
  - nested dissection
  - graph neural networks
abstract: >-
  A stealthy false-data injection attack constructed as a = Hc leaves the
  weighted-least-squares residual exactly unchanged, so the chi-square bad-data
  test detects none of them at any severity. SCEPTRE replaces message passing
  with a recursive encoder over the power network's own nested-dissection
  separator tree. Its parameter tensors are independent of the bus count, so a
  model trained on IEEE 14-bus transfers zero-shot to IEEE 118-bus with identical
  weights. Attack localization descends the same tree using split-conformal
  p-values with Benjamini-Hochberg control within each sibling family, giving
  O(k log N) node evaluations rather than the O(N) per-bus scan. The accompanying
  SSC dataset ships a per-sample physics certificate recording stealth, attacker
  cost and attacker model error, so results can be re-stratified without
  regenerating the data.
